# Jev 1.13 — findings by Iceman

- Source: TypeSafe AI / Jev 1.13 (`jev-1.13.0`)
- Date: 2026-11-14 (UTC), deep second-pass research
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Jev 1.13
- **Short description:** TypeSafe AI’s Jev 1.13 is a System One typed-decision model (not a text-generating/chat/coding LLM) that evaluates state and returns structured decisions/probabilities for software workflows.
- **Provider / access:** TypeSafe AI API (`POST /v1/systemone`, `model: jev-1.13.0` / alias contexts) and OpenCode Console listing (`jev-1.13`, `jev-1.13-free`, System One endpoint). Local metadata lists `opencode/jev-1.13`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Official TypeSafe docs list Jev 1.13 as a current model alongside Jev 1.14. Knowledge cutoff not stated in reviewed docs (decision model; not a general text-generation model).
- **IDs:** `jev-1.13`, `jev-1.13.0`, `opencode/jev-1.13`.
- **Context window:** 64k per-request / 32k per-question context by default; long-context mode (opt-in header `TypeSafe-Danger-Zone-Long-Context: true`) raises both to 262k tokens (TypeSafe docs). Local metadata notes 64K per request (32K state + 32K question); 262K opt-in via header.
- **Modalities:** Text and images input; typed decision output. Supports natural-language text state (string/JSON/arrays) and PNG/JPEG images; no native audio/video acceptance stated. Question types for Jev 1.13: Choice, Score, Noul (Box requires Jev 1.14).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** $42 per billion tokens / **$0.042 per million input tokens**; **output tokens free** (TypeSafe docs). OpenCode Console lists Jev 1.13 at $0.042/M input and free output (with free slot `jev-1.13-free`).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary TypeSafe System One decision model. Not a generative LLM; outputs typed/calibrated decisions and probabilities rather than free-form text/code/explanations.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SECOND-PASS SELF-EXCLUSION (updated): I reviewed official TypeSafe documentation (System One concepts, models page) and OpenCode Console models/pricing/docs context, plus catalog/search attempts (AA/models.dev/OpenRouter). TypeSafe provides verified product/spec/pricing/capability documentation for this exact model identity, but **no verified public benchmark numerics mapping to this project’s standard LLM evaluation dimensions** (Terminal-Bench/Tau/GDPval-AA/Toolathon/MCP-Atlas, GPQA/HLE/AIME/AA Intelligence Index/LCR, SWE-bench/LiveCodeBench/SciCode, multimodal benchmarks, etc.) were found for exact `jev-1.13`. Local metadata references “JevBench 1.5.4 score 72.13”, but this was **not independently verified** from an accessible public source in this pass and is not part of this repository’s standard comparable benchmark suite. Because Jev 1.13 is a specialized typed-decision model (not a text/code-generating LLM), assigning normalized 1–100 scores on the project’s general LLM dimensions would be misleading. This file remains `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

Agent / tool use:

- Decision/routing/triage/guardrail component for software workflows; not a general agentic text-generating model. Standard agent/tool benchmark numerics: **no verified public score found**.

Reasoning / knowledge:

- Calibrated typed decision/probability outputs over provided state/questions; not general free-form reasoning/QA generation. Standard reasoning/knowledge benchmark numerics: **no verified public score found**.

Coding:

- Cannot generate code or text responses by design (returns typed decisions). Standard coding benchmark numerics: **no verified public score found**.

Long context:

- Documented 64k/32k default and 262k opt-in long-context limits; no MRCR/RULER/AA-LCR/GraphWalks-style retrieval benchmark numerics found.

Multimodal:

- Supports image input (PNG/JPEG) in state/questions per TypeSafe docs; output is typed decisions (not multimodal generation). No standard multimodal benchmark numerics found.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not provided. Jev 1.13 is a specialized System One decision model with no verified public benchmark evidence for this project’s standard general LLM scoring dimensions; normalized LLM-category scores would be non-comparable/misleading. No scored assessment is issued and this report remains self-excluded.

### Source comparison / conflicts

- **Specs/capabilities/pricing:** TypeSafe docs and OpenCode Console listings align on core facts (System One typed-decision model, `jev-1.13.0`, Choice/Score/Noul for 1.13, text+image input, typed output, 64k/32k default and 262k opt-in, $0.042/M input with free output).
- **Benchmarks:** No verified public standard-suite benchmark numerics found for exact `jev-1.13`; metadata JevBench claim unverified.
- **Category mismatch:** Model is not a general text-generating LLM, so standard repo scoring dimensions are not directly applicable.

